[2026-05-24] Box-diffusion pipeline I3 — BoxSetDiffusionDecoder forward

- src/decoders/diffusion/box_set.py (NEW): `BoxSetDiffusionDecoder`.
  Inputs: noisy_boxes [B, N, 4] (canonical cx/cy/w/h), sigma [B],
  image_tokens [B, T, C], patch_centers [T, 2] in [-1, 1], optional
  image_key_padding_mask. Pipeline: FourierFeatures(4→D) + learned slot
  queries; image_proj(C→D) + sinusoidal PE from patch centres; K ×
  TimeFiLMTransformerBlock(self-attn + cross-attn to image); obj branch
  (FiLM-FFN + Linear→1); box branch (FiLM-FFN + cross-attn to obj_rep +
  FiLM-FFN refine + Linear→4). Outputs {pred_boxes [B,N,4],
  obj_logits [B,N]}.
- tests/test_box_set_decoder.py: 8 tests — shapes, finiteness, extreme σ
  clamp via sigma_log_offset, image key-padding mask, backward, slot-count
  validation, dim%4 validation, and (after FiLM-weight perturbation) that
  σ changes the output. All pass.
- BaseConfig wiring (`BoxSetDiffusionDecoderConfig`) deferred to I7.

[2026-05-24] Box-diffusion pipeline I2 — Fourier + TimeFiLM building blocks

- src/training/diffusion_modules.py (NEW):
  - FourierFeatures: log-spaced sin/cos bank (in_dim, num_bands, scale)
    followed by Linear→GELU→Linear. Handles scalar (σ) or vector (box coord)
    inputs. Frequencies registered as a non-persistent buffer.
  - TimeFiLMFFN: pre-norm FFN; FiLM(γ, β) drawn from time embedding via a
    zero-init Linear so the block is identity-FFN at init (training-stable).
  - TimeFiLMTransformerBlock: pre-norm self-attn + optional cross-attn +
    FiLM-FFN; supports separate `cross_dim` and `context_key_padding_mask`.
- tests/test_diffusion_modules.py: 14 unit tests covering output shapes,
  identity-at-init behaviour, FiLM activation after weight perturbation,
  backward, multi-dim Fourier input, key-padding masking. All 14 pass.

